# @container/image — first empirical witness of the @kintsugi/shift
# primitive. Arc 5 TICK 3 GREEN landing per Reed RED at `5c67af3`
# against the shift species promoted at Arc 5 TICK 2 Mara `49f0486`
# (Seam Phase D RATIFY `963f4c5`).
#
# === What this shard IS ===
#
# `@container/image` names the container-altitude view of an OCI
# image. Substrate-honest positioning: `@container/image` is NOT a
# new substrate-decl of OCI content — it is a *lens*, a *hardlink*,
# a *mount*, an *alias* onto the OCI content the substrate already
# declares at `@mirror/store/oci` altitude.
#
# Concretely: `@container/image` = `shift(@mirror/store/oci →
# @container altitude)`. Same OID at two altitudes; zero content
# duplication. This is the first empirical witness of the
# `@kintsugi/shift` primitive promoted at TICK 2 as a first-class
# substrate-decl — the primitive was promoted with four altitudes
# of prior art (portal, prism keyword, mosaic, kintsugi/surface); the
# discipline said "the substrate has been running shift for weeks."
# This shard is the first substrate-decl species that uses `shift`
# as its own load-bearing composition — not as an operation-name in
# the five-op body, but as the *shape* of the species itself. The
# species IS a shift; the species DECLARES what a shift produces at
# the target altitude.
#
# === Resolves Seam Correction #1 (`c9e153d`) via shift-form ===
#
# The Seam pre-review `c9e153d` §3 flagged Correction #1: `drop
# @container/image because it overlaps @mirror/store/oci` (would
# duplicate OCI content substrate-decl at two family-roots; violates
# the substrate's DRY discipline; risks Rice-hazard on parallel
# reinvention). The original correction was reasonable *given* the
# then-implicit assumption that `@container/image` would be a
# parallel substrate-decl of OCI content.
#
# Alex's 2026-07-06 correction: the substrate already had the word.
# `shift` IS the answer. `@container/image` does NOT duplicate
# `@mirror/store/oci` — it points AT it via `@kintsugi/shift`. The
# hardlink framing carries the discipline directly:
#
#   - Same OID (byte-equality on the underlying `shift_witness` ref;
#     the OCI content-address IS the container-altitude image's
#     identity; nothing is copied).
#   - Two altitudes (source: `@mirror/store/oci`, where OCI content
#     lives; target: `@container`, where the runtime consumes an
#     image as a rootfs source).
#   - Different reader-frame (the OCI shard sees a manifest + layer
#     descriptors; the container shard sees a materialization source
#     for `container_rootfs`).
#
# The `shift`-form resolution keeps the SURFACE the container
# runtime needs (`@container/image` as a named handle at container
# altitude, so `@container/runtime` species can compose against it
# without reaching across into `@mirror/store`) WITHOUT duplicating
# the substrate-decl of OCI content. The shift IS the composition;
# the composition IS the resolution.
#
# === Load-bearing recognition: shift as first-class species-shape ===
#
# This species stresses the substrate at the shape altitude. Every
# prior species has been a five-operation prism whose body carries a
# species-native carrier (`container_spec`, `oci_manifest`, `crystal`,
# `wasm_artifact`, etc.). @container/image inverts that: the body
# carries `image_witness` — a typed alias of `shift_witness` from
# `@kintsugi/shift` — because the species IS what a shift produces at
# the target altitude. The five operations read/produce witnesses;
# the substrate's altitude discipline rides the witness carrier; the
# species does not invent its own opaque type.
#
# This is the substrate finding out whether `@kintsugi/shift` composes
# as a species-shape and not just as an operation-name. The RED test
# suite (Reed `5c67af3`, T1-T15) drives that discipline: T7 refuses
# duplicate OCI substrate-decl at this altitude; T5 admits either a
# fresh `image_witness` type or a direct reuse of `shift_witness`;
# T6 requires the 15th composed-bilateral asserting the hardlink;
# T3+T4 require the shift-form to cite both the primitive and the
# source altitude.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #26 `shift(oid, T)` at `@mirror/spectral/portal` (Reed 2026-06-08):
#   the transport-altitude precursor of shift-as-typed-capability.
#   The portal's three `shift(oid, T)` fields carry witnesses across
#   the transport altitude; this shard carries the witness across
#   the runtime altitude.
# - #53 property/fracture bilateral pattern: this shard's
#   `image_shifted_from_oci` is the 15th composed-bilateral instance
#   (14th was `shift_preserves_content` at TICK 2; 13th was
#   `container_runnable` at TICK 1). Substrate-pull-confident.
# - #55 form/process partition: `@container` is form-side (state
#   observation: what a container image IS at runtime altitude);
#   `@kintsugi/shift` is process-side (the transformation that
#   crosses altitudes). The shift itself lives at process-side; the
#   witness it produces lives at form-side. This species names the
#   witness at the form-side target altitude.
# - #58 substrate IS Connes (A, H, D): the shift IS D (the Dirac /
#   gradient operator) crossing altitude on H (the void document);
#   `@container/image` names the projection of that gradient onto
#   the container-runtime subspace.
# - #98 candidate content-addressing cross-altitude composition:
#   this shard is a direct empirical exercise of that recognition —
#   the SHA256 OID that identifies OCI content at `@mirror/store/oci`
#   altitude is byte-identical to the OID that identifies the
#   container-altitude image; the scoping discipline differs (OCI
#   scopes to manifest+layer descriptors; container scopes to
#   rootfs-materialization source); the function is shared.
# - `substrate-already-had-the-word` (55th+ instance): the substrate
#   already had `shift`; this shard uses it rather than inventing
#   `image_lift`, `image_view`, `image_alias`, `image_ref`, or any
#   other parallel name.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   POSIX hardlink (link(2), 1988+)   two directory entries, one inode.
#                                     Exact substrate-decl of the
#                                     shift semantic at filesystem
#                                     altitude.
#   OverlayFS lower dirs (Linux 3.18) container-altitude read-only
#                                     mount of a lower filesystem;
#                                     the runtime's own hardlink of
#                                     an image's rootfs.
#   containerd snapshotter            content-addressed snapshots
#                                     that hardlink into the OCI
#                                     content store; the industry's
#                                     operational form of the same
#                                     discipline.
#   Nix store gc-roots                symlink into the CAS store;
#                                     content stays at one address,
#                                     the reader-frame differs.
#   git worktree                      one repository, many working-
#                                     tree views; same OID discipline.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]],
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]],
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]].
# Recognition ancestry: #26, #53, #55, #58, #98 candidate.
# Related shards: container.mirror (family-root; TICK 1 `aaa9a81`),
#                 kintsugi/shift.mirror (species; TICK 2 `49f0486`),
#                 io/oci.mirror (the @io distribution surface;
#                 sibling to @mirror/store/oci which is the storage
#                 surface this shard's shift points at; forward-
#                 promised as a substrate-decl species).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/container/image.mirror`
# declares `@container/image` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Does this shard use its own vocabulary correctly?
#
#   `shift` — used as: (1) species-shape (`@container/image` IS a
#   shift-form of `@mirror/store/oci`); (2) five-operation body
#   member (per prism.mirror §L38-45, basis-transformation on H);
#   (3) composed-bilateral vocabulary (`image_shifted_from_oci`
#   asserts the shift's hardlink invariant). All three uses agree:
#   same operation at three altitudes.
#
#   `witness` — the shift's altitude-invariant carrier per
#   @kintsugi/shift's `shift_witness`. `image_witness` is a typed
#   alias per [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]] — the semantic slot
#   `image at container altitude` deserves its own name even though
#   it byte-equals `shift_witness`. Explicit typing beats reuse of
#   the general carrier; the two names byte-equal at the ref altitude.
#
#   `hardlink` — used only in narrative; the substrate carries the
#   semantic through the shift's `shift_preserves_content` bilateral
#   plus this species's `image_shifted_from_oci` composed-bilateral.
#   No new substrate keyword invented; the discipline rides existing
#   carriers.
#
# Verdict: pass. Substrate-pull-realize discipline honored; no
# parallel substrate-decl invented; the shift primitive carries the
# empirical load.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @container
in @kintsugi/shift
in @mirror/store

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @container/image — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `image_witness` — a typed alias of
# `shift_witness` from `@kintsugi/shift`. Every operation on the
# species reads/produces witnesses at the container-altitude view
# of an OCI image. The substrate's altitude discipline rides the
# witness carrier; the species does not carry an opaque
# container-native content type (that would duplicate
# `@mirror/store/oci`; see T7).
prism @container/image {
  focus image_witness
  project image_witness
  split image_witness
  shift image_witness
  settle image_witness
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The witness carrier
# ============================================================

# === image_witness — the shift_witness at container-altitude ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING carrier. `image_witness` names the semantic slot
# `container-altitude view of an OCI image` per
# [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]]. It byte-equals
# `shift_witness` at the ref altitude (the OID is the same; the
# hardlink semantic guarantees the underlying bytes are shared with
# whatever the source altitude `@mirror/store/oci` handle carries)
# but the typed name distinguishes reader-frame at consumer sites.
#
# The source altitude (`@mirror/store/oci`) sees the same OID as
# `oci_content_witness` (forward-promised at that species's TDD
# tick); the target altitude sees it as `image_witness`. The two
# type names are two views of one OID; the substrate's altitude
# discipline is what distinguishes them.
#
# Composes with `@kintsugi/shift`'s `shift_witness` at the ref
# altitude: `image_witness = shift_witness` per Alex's hardlink
# framing. The realisation stores one OID; the type system reads it
# as `image_witness` at consumer sites in `@container/*` species
# (forthcoming `@container/runtime` species will consume
# `image_witness` as the rootfs materialization source).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the OCI
# content-address). The OID byte-equals across the shift crossing;
# this is exactly the `shift_preserves_content` invariant
# `@kintsugi/shift` carries at species altitude.
type image_witness = shift_witness

# ============================================================
# §3 The typed shift action at container altitude
# ============================================================

# === image — read an image at container altitude via shift ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING typed action. Consumes an `image_witness` (the
# container-altitude view of the OCI content-address) and produces
# a `container_spec` — the runtime configuration a conformant OCI
# runtime (runc / crun / gvisor / kata) admits.
#
# The realisation reads the OCI content at `@mirror/store/oci`
# altitude via the underlying OID, projects it onto the container
# altitude (basis transformation on H per
# [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]), and emits the
# `container_spec` at the target altitude. The projection composes
# with `@container`'s `container_spec` carrier (declared at
# `shards/container.mirror` §2); the shift preserves the underlying
# bytes (per `shift_preserves_content` at TICK 2) so the returned
# spec is content-addressed and byte-verifiable at the container
# altitude.
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation dispatches at
# the @io boundary (reading OCI content from `@mirror/store/oci`'s
# storage backend) but the substrate declares the shape here.
image(w: image_witness) -> container_spec { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The 15th #53 composed-bilateral
# ============================================================

# === image_shifted_from_oci — the hardlink invariant ===
#
# THE 15th INSTANCE of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]. Names the load-bearing
# invariant that resolves Seam Correction #1: the container-altitude
# image IS the shift'd view of the OCI-storage-altitude content; the
# OID persists across the altitude crossing (hardlink semantic); no
# content duplication.
#
# Composes two sub-predicates whose species-altitude realisations
# discharge the discipline:
#
#   1. `shift_preserves_content(w, @mirror/store/oci, @container, p)`
#      — the 14th composed-bilateral from `@kintsugi/shift` at
#      TICK 2. Guarantees the underlying OID byte-equals across the
#      shift (witness_oid_byte_equal sub-predicate) and both
#      altitudes are substrate-declared refs
#      (altitude_declaration_admissible sub-predicate).
#   2. `image_admissible_as_container_source(w, p)` — the shifted
#      witness is admissible as a rootfs-materialization source at
#      container altitude (composes with `container_runnable` from
#      TICK 1; the image content the shift resolves to must be
#      consumable by a conformant OCI runtime).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): both sub-predicates discharge; the image
# at container altitude IS the OCI content at storage altitude
# (byte-identical); the runtime can admit it as a rootfs source;
# the hardlink is honest.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): either sub-predicate fails;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) distinguishes:
#   - `shift_preserves_content` failure → the operation mutated
#     bytes; not a shift; belongs at `@kintsugi/morphism` or higher.
#   - `image_admissible_as_container_source` failure → the OCI
#     content is present but not consumable by an OCI runtime
#     (malformed image config, missing rootfs layers, mediaType
#     mismatch); the container altitude cannot admit it as an image
#     source pending image repair at the OCI altitude.
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): byte-equality holds modulo an
# OCI-spec-declared representation normalisation (e.g. manifest
# canonicalisation, layer compression roundtrip); confidence
# carries the normalisation magnitude. The realisation decides
# whether to admit at the graded floor.
#
# This is the 15th altitude instance of the #53 bilateral pattern
# (following container_runnable, oci_well_formed,
# stagefreight_addressable, cascade_well_defined, audit_docblock,
# shatter_round_trip, third_order_coherent, three_axis_coherent,
# and shift_preserves_content, plus five others per Taut scout).
# The pattern is substrate-pull-confident.
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation composes the
# two sub-predicate verdicts at the substrate's three-state floor
# (pass / partial(confidence) / failure(reason)).
image_shifted_from_oci(w: image_witness) -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @container/image
out image_witness
out image
out image_shifted_from_oci
